# force past a quitting player's pet. Outlaw (18) logs in, then Decimus (10), who buys a kitten (3090, @charm pet),
# quits, which saves it, and logs in again: char_list is now Decimus, his kitten, Outlaw. Smokegod (60) types
# force players quit: Decimus quits, and nuke_pets frees the kitten, which the loop had taken as its next
# character. It walked on through the free list and stopped, so Outlaw was never forced (#22). Now the loop takes
# the next player, past any mobs, before each command: both quit. Then the same again with force all.
@connect out
Outlaw
psswrd
@return
@return
@connect dec
Decimus
psswrd
@return
@return
@mob 3090 3001
@charm pet
quit
@connect dec2
Decimus
psswrd
@return
@return
@connect god
Smokegod
smoke123
@return
@return
force players quit
who
@connect out2
Outlaw
psswrd
@return
@return
@connect dec3
Decimus
psswrd
@return
@return
@as god
force all quit
who
